      "controlId": "ONE_REQUEST_ONE_TRANSACTION_ORIGIN",
      "exactRuleText": "- `ONE_REQUEST_ONE_TRANSACTION_ORIGIN`: every HTTP command path declares exactly one transaction origin; edge code never creates a transaction and participating owner calls never create a second origin.",
      "textSha256": "7db0caedf3bdb4e446d7f6aea400fa4ad6d81322b370183829757016b309e313",
      "enforcement": {
        "kind": "GATE",
        "ref": "scripts/check/backend-performance-operation-database-shape",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "enforcementPhase": "R5"
      },
      "realRedMutation": {
        "id": "BPF-U01-RED:TRANSACTION_ORIGIN",
        "purpose": "one request has one transaction origin",
        "evidence": "checker --self-test"
      }
    },
    {
      "controlId": "REQUEST_LOCAL_FACT_LOADED_ONCE",
      "exactRuleText": "- `REQUEST_LOCAL_FACT_LOADED_ONCE`: fresh authorization, session and path facts are minted once at a named request-local origin and passed as immutable facts without bypassing a current owner recheck.",
      "textSha256": "57877adae19dcb9c683070d03ec66052b9018e9c9dac7ac060d5960d3095be99",
      "enforcement": {
        "kind": "GATE",
